    {
      "name": "Why PMS symptoms show up before your period",
      "char_file": "달력_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "During the luteal phase —",
        "the two weeks before",
        "your period — progesterone drops",
        "",
        "So does allopregnanolone,",
        "a byproduct linked to",
        "more anxiety and irritability",
        "",
        "Shifting aldosterone also makes",
        "your body hold onto sodium",
        "and water, which shows up as bloating"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Skipping calcium-rich foods",
      "char_file": "우유_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Not getting enough calcium",
        "makes both the physical",
        "and mood symptoms of PMS",
        "harder to manage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Get calcium like this",
      "char_file": "치즈_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Clinical trials point to about",
        "1,200mg of calcium a day —",
        "roughly 3 to 4 servings of",
        "dairy or fortified alternatives",
        "",
        "Spread it across meals",
        "instead of one big dose at once"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Taking high-dose vitamin B6 without checking",
      "char_file": "영양제_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "The evidence for B6",
        "helping PMS symptoms is mixed",
        "",
        "Doses much above 100mg a day",
        "have been linked to",
        "nerve damage over time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Use vitamin B6 like this",
      "char_file": "알약_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "If you try it,",
        "stick to a lower dose",
        "and check the label —",
        "",
        "more isn't automatically better"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Skipping exercise because you feel drained",
      "char_file": "의자_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Feeling too drained to move",
        "is common before your period",
        "",
        "But staying inactive makes",
        "fatigue and low mood",
        "harder to shake"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Move like this instead",
      "char_file": "운동화_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Regular aerobic activity —",
        "even just brisk walking",
        "most days — eases fatigue",
        "and low mood tied to PMS",
        "",
        "likely by supporting the same",
        "brain chemicals that dip",
        "during the luteal phase"
      ]
    }
